# SHELL-L9: Linux GPUI shell product smoke.
#
# Read by scripts/linux-shell-capture.sh --actions <this file>. One step per
# line; blank lines and `#` comments are skipped. Verbs:
#   key <xdotool keystroke>   e.g. `key ctrl+t`, `key alt+Left`
#   type <text>               xdotool type (one line = one step, no newlines)
#   wait <seconds>            settle time after an action, before the next
#                             step or a `shot`
#   shot <name>               capture the window to
#                             <--name>-<name>.png
#
# Covers, in one launched shell session: omnibox navigation, back/forward,
# find-in-page, and tab open/close. Deliberately stays on internal
# `amazing://` pages (no real network fetch): the omnibox step navigates to
# `amazing://newtab`, whose demo HTML (engine_viewport.rs's NEW_TAB_HTML) has
# a `.proof` paragraph reading "AMAZING · FROM-SCRATCH BROWSER ENGINE" --
# the deterministic, always-available match the find-in-page step searches
# for. The tab-0 demo page (`amazing://status`, DEMO_HTML) that back/forward
# revisits also contains "AMAZING BROWSER ENGINE" for the same reason. The
# shell starts on tab 0; ctrl-l focuses the address bar (bound in main.rs's
# cx.bind_keys) without needing a prior click.
#
# Find-in-page runs BEFORE the tab open/close section, not after: closing a
# tab falls back to whichever tab was previously active (`close_tab`'s
# forward-then-backward search over open tabs), which on this shell's seeded
# tab strip is a pinned reference tab (TabKind::Document, e.g. "ECMA-262" --
# no `EngineViewport`, so nothing to search and nowhere to draw the find bar;
# see `find_is_available` in main.rs). Testing find while still on the
# `amazing://newtab` page it was just navigated to keeps this smoke on a tab
# that is guaranteed to have a viewport.

wait 1
shot 00-launch

# Omnibox navigation: focus the address bar, type an internal URL, commit
# with Enter -- exercises the same focus/type/commit_navigation path a real
# https:// address would, without depending on outbound network access.
key ctrl+l
wait 1
shot 01-address-bar-focused
type amazing://newtab
wait 1
key Return
wait 1
shot 02-omnibox-navigated

# Back / forward: undo that navigation (back to the tab-0 demo page), then
# redo it (back to the new-tab page).
key alt+Left
wait 1
shot 03-navigated-back
key alt+Right
wait 1
shot 04-navigated-forward

# Find in page: open the find bar (ctrl-f) while still on the new-tab page
# from the forward-navigation step above, type a query that matches its
# "AMAZING · FROM-SCRATCH BROWSER ENGINE" text, then close it (Escape).
key ctrl+f
wait 1
shot 05-find-in-page-opened
type Amazing
wait 1
shot 06-find-in-page-query-typed
key Escape
wait 1
shot 07-find-in-page-closed

# Tabs: open a new tab, then close it -- falls back to whatever tab was
# active before (see the note above; not necessarily tab 0 or the new-tab
# page), proving open/close without depending on where that lands.
key ctrl+t
wait 1
shot 08-new-tab-opened
key ctrl+w
wait 1
shot 09-tab-closed
